  clock: 1  # e3f0
  nonce: e3f0  # e3f0
  data:  # e3f0
    kind: work_item  # e3f0
    title: "astro relativizes Symbol.path against the analysis root's PARENT, so every astro path-keyed join mismatches"  # e3f0
    status: todo_hard  # e3f0
    priority: 2  # e3f0
    parent:  # e3f0
    tags:  # e3f0
    - dogfood  # e3f0
    isbefore: []  # e3f0
    duplicate_of: []  # e3f0
    not_duplicate_of: []  # e3f0
    pr_ref:  # e3f0
    description: "Every astro Symbol carries a path with one extra leading directory component, so both Symbol.path and the id path-slot disagree with every other analyzer analyzing the SAME tree.\n\nIsolated repro (one tmp dir, one analysis root, two analyzers, same call shape):\n\n    astro   path='tmp.XXXX/src/Page.astro'   id=astro:tmp.XXXX/src/Page.astro:2-2:title:variable\n    scss    path='src/a.scss'                id=scss:src/a.scss:1-1:body:rule_set\n\nastro relativizes against the analysis root's PARENT; every sibling analyzer relativizes against the root. This is not an artifact of test staging -- the two calls above share a root.\n\nCONSEQUENCE: any path-keyed join breaks for astro symbols -- the file-anchor join, per-path centrality, and the D15 invariant \"additional_file_centrality_scores subset-of node paths\". It also makes astro's own file anchor (astro:<root>/src/Page.astro:1-1:file:file) inconsistent with every sibling analyzer's anchor for the same tree.\n\nInvisible on the self-corpus: no .astro files are tracked in this repo. Found while building the INV-dulah doc-family id gate (PR #78), which is also why it is filed rather than fixed there -- it is a path-relativization defect, not an id-grammar one."  # e3f0
    fields: {}  # e3f0
- op: discuss  # 4c46
  at: '2026-10-01T00:56:47Z'  # 4c46
  by: agent  # 4c46
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 4c46
  clock: 2  # 4c46
  nonce: 4c46  # 4c46
  message: "PREMISE CHECK 2026-09-30 (dev 134a06d505): CURRENT-WITH-UPDATES (cause pinned).\n\nRepro re-run: root=astro/ with src/Page.astro + src/a.scss. analyze_astro(root) -> path\n'astro/src/Page.astro', id astro:astro/src/Page.astro:2-2:title:variable; scss -> 'src/a.scss'.\nFull run_behavior_map: astro file node path 'astro/src/Page.astro' vs scss 'src/a.scss'. Holds end-to-end.\n\nEXACT CAUSE (not in the description): astro.py:443 and :469 rebuild repo_root as\n    repo_root = file_path.parent; for _ in Path(rel_path).parts: repo_root = repo_root.parent\n-- it starts at the PARENT but walks len(parts) times, which counts the filename: off by one. The\nsame idiom in v_lang.py:163, tcl.py:175, prisma.py:97, janet.py:148, haxe.py:199 starts at\n`file_path` and is correct; astro is the only instance of the off-by-one found by\ngrep \"for _ in rel_parts\" over packages/*/src. (janet.py:145 has a dead `file_path.parent`\nassignment overwritten at :148 -- harmless.) Code is unchanged since ca20c7c5f1 (2026-02-19).\nSimplest fix: the extractor already receives rel_path; use it instead of reconstructing a root.\nNote astro also extracts each file twice (symbol pass and edge pass both call extractor.extract).\nRelated: WI-bufar (astro imports dangling dsts with too few id slots) -- same analyzer, separate cause."  # 4c46
- op: update  # 28cb
  at: '2026-10-01T01:36:24Z'  # 28cb
  by: agent  # 28cb
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 28cb
  clock: 3  # 28cb
  nonce: 28cb  # 28cb
  set:  # 28cb
    description: "Every astro Symbol carries a path with one extra leading directory component, so both Symbol.path and the id path-slot disagree with every other analyzer analyzing the SAME tree.\n\nIsolated repro (one tmp dir, one analysis root, two analyzers, same call shape):\n\n    astro   path='tmp.XXXX/src/Page.astro'   id=astro:tmp.XXXX/src/Page.astro:2-2:title:variable\n    scss    path='src/a.scss'                id=scss:src/a.scss:1-1:body:rule_set\n\nastro relativizes against the analysis root's PARENT; every sibling analyzer relativizes against the root. This is not an artifact of test staging -- the two calls above share a root. Re-measured through the full pipeline (run_behavior_map): the astro file node's path is '<root-name>/src/Page.astro' while scss's is 'src/a.scss'.\n\nCAUSE: an off-by-one in `astro.py` (lang-common) `AstroAnalyzer.extract_symbols_from_file` (:443) and `extract_edges_from_file` (:469), which rebuild the root as\n\n    repo_root = file_path.parent\n    for _ in Path(rel_path).parts: repo_root = repo_root.parent\n\nStarting at the PARENT and then stepping once per part of rel_path counts the filename, so it lands one level too high. The same idiom in v_lang.py, tcl.py, prisma.py, janet.py and haxe.py starts at `file_path` and is correct; astro is the only off-by-one instance in packages/*/src. Simplest fix: use the rel_path the extractor already receives instead of reconstructing a root. (Astro also parses each file twice -- the edge pass re-runs the extractor.)\n\nCONSEQUENCE: any path-keyed join breaks for astro symbols -- the file-anchor join, per-path centrality, and the D15 invariant \"additional_file_centrality_scores subset-of node paths\". It also makes astro's own file anchor (astro:<root>/src/Page.astro:1-1:file:file) inconsistent with every sibling analyzer's anchor for the same tree.\n\nInvisible on the self-corpus: no .astro files are tracked in this repo. Found while building the INV-dulah doc-family id gate (PR #78), which is also why it is filed rather than fixed there -- it is a path-relativization defect, not an id-grammar one.\n\nRevised 2026-09-30 from the premise check (see discussion)."  # 28cb
- op: discuss  # e1ad
  at: '2026-10-01T17:12:13Z'  # e1ad
  by: agent  # e1ad
  actor: jgstern_agent  # e1ad
  clock: 4  # e1ad
  nonce: e1ad  # e1ad
  message: "WORK DONE 2026-10-01 (decontend run): local branch jgstern-agent/fix/pifus, commit f13f35fb0f \"fix(astro): relativize paths against the analysis root, not its parent\". Not pushed, not integrated.\nFix: _AstroFileExtractor now takes the rel_path the TreeSitterAnalyzer base computed (source_file.relative_to(repo_root)) instead of re-deriving a root from the absolute path (the walk started at file_path.parent and counted the filename: one level too high). Removed the now-unused path param threading, the dead _repo_root/_run_id class attrs, and the dead analysis._astro_edges stash. Double extraction per file is NOT changed (docstring now states it).\nFamily sweep (grep \"Path(rel_path).parts\" over packages/*/src): v_lang, tcl, bitbake, janet, prisma, haxe all start at file_path and are correct (bitbake was not in the premise check's list). astro was the only off-by-one in that idiom.\nTests: test_astro.py::TestPathRelativeToAnalysisRoot (3 tests) red before the fix (3 failed: path 'test_symbol_...e0/Page.astro' != 'Page.astro'), green after. Targeted smart-test: 9047 passed, 1 xfailed, changed source at 100% coverage, mypy ratchet clean.\nLive repro after: root astroroot/ -> astro 'src/Page.astro' (was 'astroroot/src/Page.astro'), scss 'src/a.scss'.\nCorpus (nuclear, survey --include-docs, before = dev code, after = branch, fresh caches): astro nodes whose non-<external> path does not resolve under the root 31 -> 6; astro file nodes for the 8 real files now carry 'packages/website/...' (was 'nuclear/packages/website/...'); +12 contains edges (astro file -> frontmatter variable) now join; every non-astro edge identical. The 6 residual unresolved are dangling import targets built from raw relative import strings: noted on WI-modan."  # e1ad
